@copilot Replace the application-injected org.apache.hadoop.hbase.ipc.OpenTelemetryCallUtil with a normal isolated helper under io.opentelemetry.javaagent.instrumentation.hbase.client.common. Keep this work scoped to the existing HBase indy migration in this PR. The current utility uses the package-private Call type only for its class literal, casts, and instanceof, not to access any Call methods or fields. Prefer cached dynamic class lookup over injecting a helper into HBase's package solely to name that type.

Resolve org.apache.hadoop.hbase.ipc.Call once without initialization through the isolated helper's class loader, and use Class.isInstance where needed. Preserve VirtualField storage associated with the actual Call class and RequestAndContext, not Object.class or an external weak map. Follow .github/agents/knowledge/javaagent-virtual-fields.md for the dynamic carrier lookup: keep lookup outside advice in an @NoMuzzle method, cache the handle on the helper, and explicitly register the carrier/value mapping through ExperimentalInstrumentationModule.registerVirtualFields for both the HBase 1.4 and 2.0 modules. Remove the application-package utility, its injectedClassNames/isHelperClass special handling where no longer needed, and the exposedClassNames entries for RequestAndContext and HbaseRequest. Both state types should remain isolated, with no need to expose them to the application loader. No reflective member invocation, setAccessible, or injected replacement in HBase's package is needed.

Update all affected advice callers and related shared tests, including the new indy placement test and existing utility tests. Preserve request/context identity, network-peer updates on the original request, completion and timeout/error ownership guards, and clearing state after consumption. Keep HBase 1.0 behavior unchanged. Validate the affected HBase paths using the repository's targeted checks. Update any now-stale PR description about application-loaded helpers and exposed state, preserving its template and the PR's draft/ready state. Do not request another PR or expand this into unrelated changes.

